SUMMARY:Collective Liberation: A BIPOC-Led Community Event
DESCRIPTION:Psychedelic Society of Asheville\nJoin us on Saturday\, July 1
 8\, 2026\, from 11:00 AM –1:00 PM at [Third Room](https://thirdroom.art/
 ) in Asheville for a meaningful gathering rooted in connection\, healing\,
  and collective possibility.\nWe're honored to welcome [COHOBA](https://co
 hoba.org/)\, North Carolina's first psychedelic-positive\, BIPOC-led nonpr
 ofit organization based out of Charolette.\n\nCOHOBA’s work is transform
 ing the landscape of wellness through mental health services\, somatic car
 e\, creative expression\, and community-centered healing. Grounded in the 
 understanding that true wellness emerges through relationship\, culture\, 
 and collective care\, COHOBA is helping reimagine what accessible and incl
 usive healing can look like.\n\nThis special event is an opportunity to me
 et COHOBA co-founders [Laura Camilo](https://cohoba.org/our-team/)\, MSW\,
  LCSW\, and [Daniel De La Cruz](https://cohoba.org/our-team/)\, MSW\, LCSW
 \, hear the inspiring story behind their work\, and engage in meaningful c
 onversation with others who share a vision for a more connected world.\n\n
 Together\, we'll explore how communities can become powerful spaces for he
 aling\, belonging\, and transformation. We'll reflect on expanding access 
 to care\, fostering resilience\, and creating more inclusive pathways for 
 wellness and psychedelic education and exploration.\n\nWhether you're deep
 ly involved in this work or simply curious to learn more\, you'll find a w
 elcoming space where lived experience is honored\, questions are encourage
 d\, and genuine connection can flourish.\n\nThis is a donation-based event
 \, with a suggested contribution of **$15–$30**. No one will be turned a
 way due to lack of funds. Please complete your registration and submit you
 r donation via Venmo ([@psysocietyavl](https://account.venmo.com/u/psysoci
 etyavl))\, and include “COHOBA” in the payment note. Your donation dir
 ectly supports community-centered programming\, accessible healing spaces\
 , and the continued growth of COHOBA's mission and vision.\n\nCome be part
  of an afternoon of inspiration\, connection\, and collective imagination.
  We look forward to gathering with you all in Asheville.
